hadiths[94]{hadithnumber,text}:
"769","Narrated Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them): (My brother) Fadl was riding with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when a woman from the tribe of Khath'am came, and Fadl began to look at her and she began to look at Fadl. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned Fadl's face to the other side. The woman said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The obligation that Allah has placed upon His servants regarding Hajj has reached my elderly and weak father (i.e., Hajj has become obligatory upon him), but he cannot remain firm on the mount. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Yes, perform Hajj on his behalf."" And this (incident) happened during the Farewell Hajj."
"770","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mount his riding animal at Dhul-Hulaifah, and when it stood upright with him, he would say the Talbiyah."
"771","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj while riding on a camel's saddle, and his belongings were also on that same camel."
"772","Narrated by Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): She asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! We consider Jihad to be a very great act of worship, so should we not perform Jihad?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, ""No! Rather, the best Jihad is an accepted Hajj (Hajj Mabroor)."
"773","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever performs Hajj for the sake of Allah and does not utter any obscene words nor commit any sin during it, he will return (from Hajj) as free from sins as the day his mother gave birth to him."
"774","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed Dhu’l-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfah for the people of Syria, Qarn al-Manazil for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen. These places are miqat for the residents of those places as well. And whoever comes from a place other than these, intending Hajj or Umrah, and passes by these (places), then these are also his miqat. Then, whoever lives closer to Makkah than these places, he should assume ihram from where he sets out. Similarly, the people of Makkah should assume ihram from Makkah itself."
"775","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made his camel sit down in the plain of Dhul-Hulaifah, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer there, and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to do the same."
"776","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when going for Hajj, would take the route of Shajarah and would return by the route of Mu'arras. And indeed, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go towards Makkah, he would pray in the mosque of Shajarah, and when returning, he would pray in Dhul-Hulaifah, which is situated in the middle of the valley, and then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend the night there until morning."
"777","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saying in the valley of Aqiq: ""Last night, a messenger from my Lord came to me and said (to me): Pray in this blessed valley (i.e., Aqiq) and say: 'I have entered into the state of Ihram for both Hajj and Umrah (because Umrah has been included in Hajj. Umrah can also be performed during the days of Hajj).'"
"778","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shown this dream in the last part of the night when he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was staying near Mu'arris at Dhul-Hulaifah, and it was said to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that at this time he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is in a blessed valley. (Remember that the dreams of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are also included in revelation.)"
"779","Sayyiduna Ya’la bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), “Show me the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the state when revelation is being sent down to him.” So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Alright.” Ya’la (may Allah be pleased with him) says that in that state, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the place of Ji’ranah when a man came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah! What is your command regarding a person who has put on the Ihram for ‘Umrah while he is scented with perfume?” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent for a while. Then revelation began to descend upon him, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) signaled to Ya’la (may Allah be pleased with him), so he came, and at that time a cloth was spread over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), providing shade over him. So Ya’la (may Allah be pleased with him) put his head under that cloth and saw that the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was red and he was snoring. Then that state was lifted from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said, “Where is the man who asked about ‘Umrah?” That man was brought, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Wash off the perfume that you have applied three times, and take off your cloak from your body, and perform the acts of ‘Umrah just as you do in Hajj.”"
"780","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) (the wife of the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him) says: ""I used to apply perfume to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) at the time of putting on Ihram, and similarly, when he would end the Ihram before performing the Tawaf al-Ziyarah (I would apply perfume to him at that time as well)."
"781","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the state that he was calling out the Talbiyah with his hair matted together."
"782","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not recite the Talbiyah (i.e., Labbaik) after assuming Ihram except near the mosque, that is, near the mosque of Dhul-Hulaifah."
"783","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that from Arafah to Muzdalifah, Sayyiduna Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) was riding with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Then from Muzdalifah to Mina, Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) rode with him. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that both (companions) stated that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to recite the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"784","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions, after combing their hair, applying oil, wearing a sheet, and tying a waist-wrapper, set out from Madinah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not prohibit wearing any kind of sheet or waist-wrapper except for clothes dyed with saffron from which saffron would fall onto the body. Then in the morning, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted his ride at Dhul-Hulaifah, and when he reached (the place) Bayda, his companions proclaimed the Talbiyah and put garlands on the necks of their sacrificial animals, and at that time, five days of the month of Dhul-Qa'dah remained. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) reached Makkah on the fourth of Dhul-Hijjah, performed Tawaf of the Ka'bah, and performed Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, and he did not come out of Ihram because of his sacrificial animals, as he had already put garlands on their necks. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed at the elevated place of Makkah near (the place) Hajun, and he was in the state of Ihram for Hajj. After performing Tawaf, he did not go near the Ka'bah until he returned from Arafah. And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered his companions to perform Tawaf of the Ka'bah and Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, then cut their hair and come out of Ihram. But this command was only for the one who did not have a sacrificial animal with him or had not put a garland on the animal's neck, and after cutting the hair, whoever had his wife with him, it became permissible for him to have intercourse, apply perfume, and wear clothes."
"785","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the following Talbiyah: ""O Allah! Here I am at Your service, here I am at Your service. There is no partner with You. All praise and bounty are Yours, and the sovereignty is Yours. There is no partner with You."
"786","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered four rak‘ahs of Zuhr prayer in Madinah, and we were with him. Then, when he reached Dhul-Hulaifah at the time of ‘Asr, he offered two rak‘ahs. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Dhul-Hulaifah for the whole night until morning came. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted (his ride), and when his mount reached Al-Baida’, he praised Allah, glorified Him, and proclaimed His greatness. After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronounced the Talbiyah for both Hajj and ‘Umrah, and the people also pronounced the Talbiyah for both Hajj and ‘Umrah. Then, when we reached (Makkah), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the people to come out of the state of Ihram, so they came out of Ihram until the day of Tarwiyah came, and the people entered into Ihram for Hajj. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered several camels with his own hand while standing, and in Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two rams with horns."
"787","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)` would begin reciting the Talbiyah (Labbaik) from Dhul-Hulaifah and would stop upon reaching the Haram. He would spend the night at the place of Dhi Tuwa until morning, then after performing the Fajr prayer, he would take a bath and say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do the same."
"788","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about Musa (peace be upon him): ""It is as if I am seeing him at this moment, when he was descending into the valley, reciting the Talbiyah."
"789","´Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me to my people in Yemen. When I returned, I found that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was in Batha. He (peace and blessings be upon him) asked me, ""With what intention did you enter into Ihram?"" I replied, ""I entered into Ihram in the same way as the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Do you have a sacrificial animal with you?"" I replied, ""No."" So he (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered me to perform Tawaf of the Ka'bah. Accordingly, I performed Tawaf of the Ka'bah and (Sa'i) between Safa and Marwah. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered me to come out of Ihram, so I came out of Ihram. Then I went to a woman from my people and she combed my hair or washed my head. Later, when Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) became the Caliph (and I narrated this hadith to him), he said, ""We do not know what kind of hadith this is. If we act upon the Book of Allah, it commands us to complete Hajj and Umrah, as Allah the Exalted has said (Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 196): 'And complete the Hajj and Umrah for Allah.' And if we act upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then he (peace and blessings be upon him) did not come out of Ihram until he had offered the sacrifice."
"790","The hadith of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding Hajj has already been mentioned (see the Book: Statement of Menstruation... Chapter: Concerning the Issues of Menstruation When a Woman is Menstruating...). And here in this narration, she says that we set out (from Madinah) in the months of Hajj, during the nights of Hajj, in the state of Ihram for Hajj. Then we stopped at (the place) Sarif. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to his companions and said: “Whoever among you does not have a sacrificial animal with him and wishes to perform Umrah with this Ihram, let him do so. And whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him not do so.” Umm al-Mu’minin says, so some of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted upon this command and some did not. She further says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and some of his companions had the means and ability, and those who had sacrificial animals with them were not able to perform Umrah (i.e., they could not exit Ihram after Umrah), and then she narrated the rest of the hadith."
"791","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that we set out from Madinah with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we had only the intention of Hajj (i.e., we had put on the Ihram for Hajj). Then, when we reached Makkah and had performed the Tawaf of the Ka’bah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that whoever did not have a sacrificial animal should come out of the state of Ihram. So those who did not have a sacrificial animal came out of Ihram, and the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also did not have a sacrificial animal, so they too came out of Ihram. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that due to menstruation, I could not perform the Tawaf of the House (Ka’bah). When the night of Hasab came, I said, “O Messenger of Allah! People will return after performing both Umrah and Hajj, but I will return after performing only Hajj.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Did you not perform Tawaf when you came to Makkah?” I said, “No.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Go with your brother to Tan’eem, put on the Ihram for Umrah from there, and after completing the Umrah, meet us at such-and-such place.” Umm al-Mu’minin Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “I think I am holding all of you back.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “O barren one, did you not perform Tawaf on the day of sacrifice?” Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “Yes, I did.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Then there is no harm, let us go.”"
"792","In another narration from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), it is stated that we set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage (towards Makkah). Some of us assumed ihram for ‘Umrah, some assumed ihram for both ‘Umrah and Hajj, and some assumed ihram for only Hajj. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) assumed ihram for Hajj. So whoever assumed ihram for Hajj or for both Hajj and ‘Umrah did not come out of ihram until the day of sacrifice arrived."
"793","`Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)` (during his caliphate) used to prohibit performing Tamattu‘ and Qiran (combining Hajj and ‘Umrah). So when Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) saw this, he put on the Ihram for both Hajj and ‘Umrah together and said: ((Labbayka bi ‘umratin wa hajjatin)) (that is, he performed Qiran), and said that I cannot abandon the Sunnah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of anyone’s statement."
"794","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that (in the days of ignorance) people used to think that performing Umrah during the days of Hajj was worse than all the evils in the world, and they would consider the month of Muharram as the month of Safar, and would say that when the wound on the camel’s back (which often occurred due to the saddle being tied on it during the journey of Hajj) healed and the mark completely disappeared and Safar had passed, then at that time Umrah was permissible for the one who wished to perform Umrah. So when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the companions, having donned the Ihram for Hajj on the morning of the fourth of Dhul-Hijjah, arrived in Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the companions to break this Ihram and instead assume Ihram for Umrah. This seemed bad to those people, and they said, “O Messenger of Allah! What should we do to come out of Ihram?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Everything.”"
"795","Umm al-Mu'mineen Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him), asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is the matter with the people that they have come out of ihram after performing 'umrah, but you (peace be upon him) have not come out of ihram after performing 'umrah?"" The Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, ""I have matted my hair and put a garland on my sacrificial animal, therefore I cannot come out of ihram until I have performed the sacrifice."
"796","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man asked him about Tamattu’ and said that people had forbidden him from it. So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) instructed him to perform Tamattu’ with peace of mind. The man said, “Then I saw in a dream as if someone was saying to me: ‘Hajj is excellent and ‘Umrah is accepted.’” So I related this dream to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he said, “This is the Sunnah of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), (do it with eagerness).”"
"797","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he performed Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he (the Prophet) had brought the sacrificial animal with him, and all the companions had assumed Ihram for Hajj Mufrad. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: ""You people should perform Tawaf of the Ka'bah and Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, then come out of Ihram and cut your hair, then remain out of Ihram until the eighth (of Dhul-Hijjah), then you should assume Ihram for Hajj, and the Ihram with which you have come, make it for Tamattu'."" The companions said: Should we make it Tamattu' even though we have mentioned Hajj (in our intention)? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do whatever I command you. If I had not brought the sacrificial animal, I would have done as I am commanding you, but now I cannot come out of Ihram until the sacrificial animal reaches its place of sacrifice."
"798","Narrated Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him): We performed (Hajj) Tamattu‘ during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the same command regarding it was revealed in the Qur’an, but a person said whatever he wished according to his own opinion."
"799","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter Makkah from the direction of Kada’, that is, from the high pass which is in Batha, and when leaving Makkah, he would go out from the lower pass."
"800","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about the Hatim wall, whether it is also part of the Ka’bah? He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “Yes.” I asked: Then why did those people not include it within the Ka’bah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Your people had insufficient funds (that is why they did not include it).” I asked: What is the matter with the door? Why is it so high? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Your people did this so that they could allow into the Ka’bah whomever they wished and prevent whomever they wished. And if your people were not so close to the time of ignorance, and if I did not fear that their hearts would dislike it, I would certainly have included the Hatim within the Ka’bah and lowered its door to the ground (that is, made the threshold lower).”"
"801","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), if your people had not recently left the Age of Ignorance, I would have ordered the Ka'bah to be demolished, and I would have included in it the part that was left out, and I would have joined it with the ground, and I would have made two doors for it—one eastern door and one western door—and I would have made it according to the foundations of Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"802","Narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When he was going for the Farewell Pilgrimage, he submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! Where will you stay in your house in Makkah?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Aqeel has not left any property or houses (for us)."" And Aqeel and Talib became the heirs of Abu Talib, neither Sayyiduna Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) inherited anything from him, nor Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), because both of them were Muslims and Aqeel and Talib (at that time) were disbelievers."
"803","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day after sacrifice, that is, on the eleventh of Dhul-Hijjah, while he was in Mina: ""Tomorrow, if Allah wills, we will stay at Khayf Bani Kinana, where the polytheists made a pact of disbelief among themselves, that is, we will stay at Muhassab. And this incident (the pact of disbelief) happened in such a way that the Quraish and Kinana made an agreement against Bani Hashim and Bani Abdul Muttalib (or the narrator said: Bani Muttalib) that they would not marry with them nor sell them anything until Bani Hashim handed over the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to them."
"804","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""A man from Abyssinia with thin legs will demolish the Ka'bah (near the Day of Judgment)."
"805","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: (We) used to fast on the day of Ashura before the fasting of Ramadan was made obligatory, and it was a day on which the covering was placed over the Ka'bah. Then, when Allah Almighty made Ramadan obligatory, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(Now) whoever wishes to fast on Ashura may do so, and whoever does not wish to fast may leave it."
"806","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Even after the emergence of Gog and Magog, Hajj and 'Umrah of the Ka'bah will be performed."
"807","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""It is as if I am seeing that thin-legged, dark-skinned (i.e., Abyssinian) man who will dismantle the Ka'bah stone by stone."
"808","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he came to the Black Stone (during Tawaf), then he kissed it and said: ""Indeed, I know that you are a stone; you can neither harm nor benefit anyone. And if I had not seen the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would never have kissed you."
"809","Narrated Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ‘Umrah, then circumambulated the Ka‘bah and prayed two rak‘ahs behind Maqam Ibrahim. At that time, there was a man with him who was shielding him from the people. Then a person asked Abdullah bin Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him): “Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) enter the Ka‘bah?” He replied, “No.”"
"810","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came (for Hajj), he refused to enter the Ka'bah, and (the reason was that) there were idols placed inside it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that those idols be removed from there. Then people took out pictures of Ibrahim and Isma'il (peace be upon them) from inside (the idol), and in the hands of both of them were arrows for drawing lots. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah destroy these people! By Allah, they know that Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and Isma'il (peace be upon him) never drew lots with arrows."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbeer around the Ka'bah and did not pray inside it."
"811","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his companions came (to Makkah for Hajj), the polytheists (before his arrival) started saying among themselves that now a group is coming to us whom the fever of Yathrib has weakened. So (upon hearing this), the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered them to perform ramal (brisk walk) in three circuits and to walk normally between the two Yemeni corners. And the reason why the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not order them to perform ramal in all the circuits was to make things easy for the people; there was no other reason for this."
"812","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered Makkah, he would kiss the Black Stone in the first circuit of Tawaf and would perform Ramal (brisk walking) in three out of the seven circuits."
"813","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: What concern did we have with ramal? The only thing was that we showed our strength to the polytheists, and (now) Allah the Exalted has destroyed them. Then he said: We do not wish to abandon any act which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed."
"814","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says:` I have never abandoned touching these two Yemeni corners, whether in difficult circumstances or ease (in any situation), since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) touching them."
"815","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf during the Farewell Hajj while riding his camel, and he kissed the Black Stone with a stick. (That is, he touched the Black Stone with a stick and then kissed it.)"
"816","A person asked Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) about kissing the Black Stone, so he replied: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) touching it and kissing it. The person said, ""Tell me, if there is a crowd, (or) if people overpower me, then how should I kiss the Black Stone?"" He replied, ""Leave these ifs and buts in Yemen; I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) kissing it and touching it."
"817","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the very first act which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did upon arriving in Mecca was that he performed ablution, then performed Tawaf, and at that time, only performing Tawaf did not constitute Umrah. Then the Commander of the Faithful Abu Bakr Siddiq and our master Umar Farooq (may Allah be pleased with them both) also performed Hajj in the same manner."
"818","The hadith regarding Tawaf narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) has just been mentioned (see the chapter: Upon arriving in Makkah, it is Sunnah to kiss the Black Stone and perform ramal in the first three circuits of the initial Tawaf...). In this narration, it is further stated that after performing Tawaf, he would offer two rak'ahs, then perform Sa'i between Safa and Marwah."
"819","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that while performing Tawaf of the Ka'bah, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a man who had tied his hand with a strap or rope or something else, and another person was pulling him by it. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) broke that rope with his own hand and then said: ""Lead him by holding his hand."
"820","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): Abu Bakr As-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) sent me during that Hajj in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had appointed him as the leader before the Farewell Pilgrimage, along with a group of people, to announce to the people on the Day of Sacrifice that: ""After this year, no polytheist shall perform Hajj, nor shall any naked person circumambulate the Ka'bah."
"821","Narrated Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, performed Tawaf, and performed Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. After this Tawaf, he did not go near the Ka'bah until he returned from Arafat (then he went near the Ka'bah)."
"822","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) requested the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for permission to stay in Makkah during the nights of Mina in order to provide water to the pilgrims, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted him permission."
"823","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the Sabeel and asked for Zamzam water. So Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said (to his son), ""O Fadl! Go to your mother and bring water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Give me this water to drink."" Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! People put their hands in it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Give me to drink from this itself."" So he (the Prophet) drank from it. Then he came to the place of Zamzam, and there people were drawing water from the well and giving it to others to drink. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""If it were not that you would be overpowered (i.e., the task of giving water would be taken from your hands), then surely I would descend and, pointing to his shoulder, said, I would place the rope on my shoulder (and draw water myself), but I think that if I do so, others, out of obedience, would also do the same, and then you would be overpowered."
"824","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that: I gave Zamzam water to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink, so he drank it while standing. In another narration, Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was riding a camel that day."
"825","‘From Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), her nephew Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) asked her about the saying of Allah Almighty: “Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs Umrah, there is no blame upon him for walking between them.” (Surah Al-Baqarah: 158), and he said, “By Allah! From this it seems (to me) that there is no sin upon anyone if he does not perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwah?” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) replied, “O nephew! You have stated a very wrong meaning. If the meaning was as you have stated, then the verse would have been: ‘Indeed, there was no sin upon anyone for not walking between them.’ Rather, this verse was revealed about the Ansar. Before accepting Islam, they used to assume Ihram for ‘Manat’ (an idol) kept near Mushallal, and people used to worship it. And those among the Ansar who assumed Ihram for Hajj or Umrah used to consider it a sin to perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwah. So when they became Muslims, they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah! We used to consider it objectionable to perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwah.’ So Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ‘Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah...’ until the end of the verse.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established the practice of Sa’i between them, so no one has the option to abandon Sa’i between them.”"
"826","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when performing the first Tawaf, used to walk briskly (raml) for three circuits and walk normally for four circuits, and when performing Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, he would hasten in the dip of the valley."
"827","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions assumed the Ihram for Hajj, and none of them had a sacrificial animal except the Prophet (peace be upon him) and Sayyiduna Talha (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came from Yemen and he had a sacrificial animal with him. So he said, ""I have assumed Ihram for the same thing for which the Prophet (peace be upon him) has assumed Ihram."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered the companions: ""Change this Ihram to the Ihram of Umrah, perform Tawaf, cut your hair, and come out of Ihram, except for the one who has a sacrificial animal with him."" Then the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""How can we go to Mina while semen will be dripping from our private parts?"" This news reached the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he said: ""If I had known earlier what I have come to know now, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal with me, and if I did not have the sacrificial animal with me, I would have come out of Ihram."
"828","A person (Abdul Aziz bin Rafee’) asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), “Tell me something that you remember from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): where did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) offer the Zuhr and Asr prayers on the eighth day of Dhul-Hijjah?” He replied, “At Mina.” The person asked again, “On the day of departure (the twelfth), where did he offer the Asr prayer?” He replied, “At Abtah.” Then Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “You should do as your leaders do.”"
"829","`Umm Fadl (may Allah be pleased with her)` (the aunt of the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him) says that on the day of Arafah, people were in doubt about whether the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, was fasting. So I sent something for the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, to drink, and he drank it (thus it became known that he was not fasting)."
"830","´Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)´ came near the tent of Hajjaj after the sun had declined on the day of Arafah and called out in a loud voice, so Hajjaj came out, and he was wearing a cloak dyed with safflower. Hajjaj said (to Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both), ""O Abu Abdur Rahman! What is the matter?"" He replied, ""If you want to follow the Sunnah, then you should proceed (for Wuquf)."" Hajjaj asked, ""Right now?"" He said, ""Yes."" Hajjaj said, ""Give me a little time so that I may pour water over my head and then proceed."" So Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) dismounted from his ride (and waited) until Hajjaj came out. Then he began to walk between me (Salim bin Abdullah) and my respected father (Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both). (Salim bin Abdullah says) I said to Hajjaj, ""If you want to follow the Sunnah, then keep the sermon short and hasten in Wuquf."" So Hajjaj began to look towards Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both). When Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saw this, he said, ""He (Salim) is right."" And Abdul Malik (the king of Sham) had written to Hajjaj (who was the governor and Makkah was also under his control) that he should not oppose Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) in Hajj."
"831","Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) says that (before accepting Islam) on the day of Arafah, one of my camels was lost. I went out to search for it, and I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at Arafat. So I said to myself, “By Allah, he is from the people of Hums (the strict people, i.e., the Quraysh), so what is he doing here?”"
"832","It was asked from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him): When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) departed from Arafat during the Farewell Pilgrimage, how was he walking? Sayyiduna Usama (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: Even in the crowd, he was walking briskly, and when the ground was clear, he would walk even faster. The narrator (Hisham bin Urwah) says that ""nas"" (means walking faster) is more than ""anaq"" (brisk walking)."
"833","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that on the day of Arafah, he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (on the return from Arafat). He says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) heard a lot of noise and the sound of people striking their camels behind him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gestured towards them with his whip and said: ""O people! Maintain calmness, for making the camels run fast is not a virtue."
"834","Narrated from Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) that she stayed near Muzdalifah on the night of Muzdalifah and stood up to pray. After praying for a short while, she asked, ""O son! Has the moon set?"" (Abdullah) said, ""No."" So she continued to pray for a little while. After that, she asked, ""O son! Has the moon set?"" (Abdullah) said, ""Yes."" Then she said, ""Let us go now."" So we departed and continued until Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) reached Mina and threw the pebbles, then came to her place and offered the morning prayer there. I (Abdullah) said to her, ""Madam! We think that we have hastened."" Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) replied, ""O son! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had already given permission for this to women."
"835","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: We stopped at Muzdalifah, so Umm al-Mu'mineen Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to depart before the crowd of people, and she was a woman of heavy build. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her permission, and she departed before the crowd of people, while we remained there until morning came. Then we set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (But I was so distressed that I wished) if only I had also sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) had done, that would have been dearer to me than any happiness."
"836","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he went to Muzdalifah along with all the people. There, Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) performed two prayers together (Maghrib and ‘Isha). He only offered the obligatory (fard) prayers of each, with adhan and iqamah, and ate food between the two prayers. After that, when dawn began, he immediately performed the Fajr prayer. At that time, it was so dark that some people said Fajr had begun and others said it had not yet begun. After completing the prayer, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “These two prayers, at this place, i.e., Muzdalifah, have been delayed from their (original) times—Maghrib and ‘Isha. So people should not come to Muzdalifah until the time of ‘Isha, and the Fajr prayer should be performed early in the morning at its (proper) time.” Then Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) stayed until the whiteness (of morning) spread widely. After that, he said: If the Commander of the Faithful, ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), were to proceed now towards Mina, he would be acting in accordance with the Sunnah. (When the Commander of the Faithful, may Allah be pleased with him, departed, the narrator ‘Abdur Rahman says:) I do not know whether the statement of Sayyiduna Ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) came first or the departure of the Commander of the Faithful, Sayyiduna ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) came first. Then Sayyiduna Ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) continued reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-‘Aqabah on the day of sacrifice. (At that time, he stopped the Talbiyah.)"
"837","‘Ameer-ul-Mu’mineen Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) offered the Fajr prayer at Muzdalifah, then remained there. After that he said: “The polytheists would not depart from here until the sun had risen, and they used to say: ‘O Thubair!’ (the name of a mountain) ‘Shine with the rays of the sun.’ And indeed, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opposed them in this matter.” After that, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) departed before the sun had risen."
"838","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial animal, so he (peace be upon him) said: ""Ride on it."" He said, (O Messenger of Allah!) this is a sacrificial animal (how can I ride on it?). So he (peace be upon him) said: ""Ride on it."" He again said, this is a sacrificial animal. Then for the second or third time, he (peace be upon him) said: ""Woe to you, ride on it."
"839","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Tamattu’ in the Farewell Hajj with ‘Umrah and Hajj together and brought the sacrificial animal with him. So he brought the sacrificial animal from Dhul-Hulaifah and first put on the Ihram for ‘Umrah, then after that put on the Ihram for Hajj. Thus, other people also performed Tamattu’ with ‘Umrah and Hajj along with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in his following, and some of them brought sacrificial animals and some did not. So when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Makkah, he said to the people: “Whoever among you has brought the sacrificial animal should avoid what is avoided in Ihram until the Hajj is completed, and whoever has not brought it should perform Tawaf of the Ka’bah and Sa’i between Safa and Marwah, cut his hair, and come out of Ihram. After that, on the seventh or eighth of Dhul-Hijjah, he should put on Ihram only for Hajj (then perform Hajj and offer sacrifice). Then whoever cannot find a sacrificial animal should fast three days during the days of Hajj and seven days when he returns home.”"
"840","Narrated from Sayyiduna Miswar bin Makhrama and Marwan (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) set out for the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah with more than a thousand companions, until when he reached Dhul-Hulaifah, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) put a garland around the neck of the sacrificial animal and marked it with a slight wound using a knife, and assumed the Ihram for Umrah."
"841","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she heard that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: Whoever sends a sacrificial animal to the Ka'bah, all those things become forbidden for him which are forbidden for a pilgrim, until his sacrifice is offered. Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: What Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) has said is not correct, because I myself tied the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my own hands. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put those garlands on the animals with his own hands, then sent those animals along with my father (Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him), but nothing which Allah had made lawful for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became forbidden for him until the sacrifice of the animals."
"842","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent goats for sacrifice. And in another narration, it is stated that he (peace and blessings be upon him) would send the goats after putting collars on them, while he himself remained in his house in a state of being non-muhrim (not in the state of ihram)."
"843","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I made necklaces for the sacrificial animals from the cotton that I had."
"844","Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me to give away in charity the saddles and skins of the animals that were sacrificed."
"845","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: We set out from Madinah on the 25th of Dhu al-Qa'dah... This hadith has already been mentioned before (see the chapter: The explanation of Tamattu', Qiran, and Ifrad Hajj, and the permission for one who does not have a sacrificial animal to change his Hajj into 'Umrah...). Here, in this narration, it is further mentioned that on the day of sacrifice, beef was brought before us, so I asked, ""What kind of meat is this?"" The one who brought it replied, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered a sacrifice on behalf of his wives."
"846","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)` used to offer sacrifice at the place of sacrifice, that is, at the place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer sacrifice."
"847","`Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) passed by a man who had made his animal (camel) sit down in order to slaughter it. So he said, ""Make it stand and tie its leg (and then slaughter it), for this is the Sunnah of Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"848","Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed me to supervise the sacrificial camels and not to give the butcher anything from them as wages."
"849","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): We used to not eat the meat of sacrifice for more than three days, and that too only in Mina (it was prohibited to take the meat outside Mina). After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted us permission and said: ""Eat and take it with you."" So we ate and brought it along."
"850","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had his head shaved during his Hajj."
"851","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Have mercy on those who shave their heads."" The companions submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! (Pray for mercy) for those who trim their hair as well."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Send mercy upon those who shave their heads."" The companions again submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! (Pray for mercy) for those who trim their hair as well."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the third time) said: ""And (have mercy) on those who trim their hair as well."
"852","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O Allah! Forgive those who shave their heads."" The companions said: ""And those who trim their hair as well."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, repeated: ""O Allah! Forgive those who shave their heads."" The companions said: ""And those who trim their hair as well."" Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said for the third time: ""And forgive those who trim their hair as well."
"853","`Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I trimmed the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with scissors."
"854","A man asked `Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)` at what time should he throw the pebbles at the Jamarat. He replied: ""At the time your Imam throws, you should also throw."" The man asked him the same question again, so he replied: ""We used to wait, and when the sun would decline (past midday), then we would throw the pebbles."
"855","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) that he threw pebbles from the lower part of the valley, so he was asked that some people throw from the upper part of the valley. Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) replied, ""By Him besides whom there is no true deity! This is the place of throwing (rami) of that person (i.e., Muhammad, peace be upon him) upon whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed."
"856","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that when he reached the big Jamrah, he kept the Ka'bah to his left and Mina to his right, and stoned with seven pebbles. He said: ""This is how the person upon whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed (ﷺ) performed the stoning."
"857","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he would throw seven pebbles at the first Jamrah, saying Takbeer after each pebble. Then he would move forward until he reached level ground, face the Qiblah, stand for a long time, raise his hands, and make supplication. Then he would perform the Rami of the middle Jamrah, then move to the left, and upon reaching level ground, he would face the Qiblah, stand, raise his hands, and make supplication, remaining standing in this manner. Then, from the lower part of the valley, he would throw pebbles at Jamrah Aqabah and would not stay there but would return, and he used to say: I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing this."
"858","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that people were instructed on behalf of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that their last act (before leaving Makkah) should be with the Ka'bah (i.e., they should perform Tawaf of the Ka'bah before departing), but this was excused for a menstruating woman."
"859","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha prayers at (the place of) Muhassab, then rested for a short while. After that, he rode towards the Ka'bah and performed its Tawaf."
"860","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says` A woman who becomes menstruating after performing the Tawaf al-Ifadah, it is permissible for her to leave Makkah. (Tawoos) says that I heard Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) saying that she should not leave Makkah, but finally I heard him saying that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had permitted menstruating women to leave."
"861","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that´ staying at Muhassab (is neither among the rites of Hajj nor) is it any act of worship; it is merely a place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to stay. Before entering Makkah, (the place) Dhi Tuwa, which is adjacent to Makkah, and when returning from Makkah to Madinah, staying in that stony field (Batha) which is in Dhul-Hulaifah."
"862","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when he would go to Makkah, he would stay at Dhi Tuwa until morning came, then he would enter Makkah. And when he returned from Makkah, he would also stay at Dhi Tuwa and spend the night there until morning came. And he used to state that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do the same."
